body:
Fixes #335.

Follow-up for #335.

What changed:
- service/attach runtimes still merge `DiscoveryQueryPeers` into bootstrap peers before startup, so private service runtimes can reach the cluster authority/discovery peer without relying on relay pubsub fallback;
- service advertisement now fails closed if `<service>.membership.cap.json` is missing;
- service advertisement no longer falls back to namespace- or cluster-scoped membership capability files;
- `grants serve` now recomputes `p2p.PeerAddrs(h)` and `overlay.ReachableAddrs()` on every grant-service discovery wait poll;
- attach now signs `AnnouncementV3` before both PubSub publish and direct authority sync;
- announce rejection logging now surfaces `announce_v3` / grant-service sync rejections directly in logs.

Root cause fixed:
- the remaining #336 blocker was that default `tubo get services` stayed empty after attach approval even though attach was running advertised/authorized;
- attach heartbeat PubSub-published a signed `AnnouncementV3`;
- direct authority sync used the original unsigned `AnnouncementV3`;
- the authority rejected it with `validate announcement_v3: announcement signature invalid`;
- as a result, the authority cache kept `grant-service` but dropped the attached user service from default discovery results.

Evidence:
- Branch: `issue-335-grant-service-bootstrap`
- Commit: `14e252d`
- Focused regression now passes:
  - `go test ./cmd/tubo -run 'TestPublishedServiceBecomesQueryableAndVisibleInDefaultListings'`
- That regression proves:
  - authority sees `grant-service`;
  - attached user service becomes queryable;
  - default listing shows the user service;
  - `--system` still shows only `grant-service`.

Test status:
- Changed-area tests run:
  - `go test ./internal/workspace ./internal/attachauth ./internal/app/service ./cmd/tubo`
- Focused regression run:
  - `go test ./cmd/tubo -run 'TestPublishedServiceBecomesQueryableAndVisibleInDefaultListings'`
- Full suite run:
  - `go test ./...`
- Local `go test ./...` is still red only for failures reproduced on `main`:
  - multiple `cmd/tubo` process/cmdline tests fail the same way on `main` in this environment (`process ... did not exit in time`, `expected current process cmdline`);
  - `TestSecretBackedDiscoveryObserveServicesHandlesMismatchAndRotation` is preexisting/flaky and also fails on `main` with the same discovery-rotation error when run in isolation.

Conclusion:
- The #336 discovery blocker is fixed.
- Public relay GossipSub is still unnecessary for the private discovery path.
- With the blocker removed and only main-reproducible failures remaining locally, this PR is ready for review.
